## 99. Golden Rule: Simplest Consistent Rule

If:

```text
CAT → DBU
```

do not invent:

```text
matrix
+ prime numbers
+ reversal
+ multiplication
```

when:

```text
+1
```

already explains everything.

Use:

> The simplest rule that explains **all** examples.

---

## 100. Rule Verification

Never stop after finding a rule from one letter.

If:

```text
CAT → DBU
```

you think:

```text
+1
```

Verify all three:

```text
C → D ✓
A → B ✓
T → U ✓
```

Then test another provided example if available.

---

## 101. Two-Example Verification

Suppose:

```text
DOG → EPH
CAT → DBU
```

Check:

```text
D→E +1
O→P +1
G→H +1

C→D +1
A→B +1
T→U +1
```

Now the rule is strongly confirmed.

---

## 102. Contradiction Detection

Suppose:

```text
CAT → DBU
DOG → EPH
```

but a proposed rule says:

```text
first letter +1
second letter +2
third letter +1
```

Check:

```text
CAT
C→D +1
A→C +2
T→U +1
```

This predicts:

```text
DCU
```

not:

```text
DBU
```

Therefore reject the rule.

---

## 103. Coding Solving Algorithm

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Read all examples] --> B[Separate input and output]
    B --> C[Convert letters to positions]
    C --> D[Calculate differences]
    D --> E{Simple rule?}
    E -->|Yes| F[Verify on every example]
    E -->|No| G[Check reversal / rearrangement]
    G --> H[Check alternating or position rules]
    H --> I[Check word properties]
    I --> J[Check mathematical transformation]
    J --> F
    F --> K{All examples fit?}
    K -->|Yes| L[Apply rule]
    K -->|No| G
```

---

## 104. Master Solving Flowchart

```text
                 START
                   |
                   ↓
           Read ALL examples
                   |
                   ↓
        Separate INPUT / OUTPUT
                   |
                   ↓
       ┌───────────────────────┐
       │ Letter positions?     │
       └──────────┬────────────┘
                  ↓
        Calculate differences
                  |
         ┌────────┴────────┐
         ↓                 ↓
    Constant shift?      No
         |                 |
        YES                ↓
         |          Reverse alphabet?
         |                 |
         |          ┌──────┴──────┐
         |          ↓             ↓
         |         YES            NO
         |          |             |
         |          |      Position pattern?
         |          |             |
         └──────────┴─────────────┤
                                   ↓
                            Word properties?
                                   |
                                   ↓
                            Math / sequence?
                                   |
                                   ↓
                              VERIFY ALL
                                   |
                                   ↓
                                ANSWER
```

---

## 105. Advanced Pattern: Pairwise Operations

Letters may be grouped:

```text
AB CD EF
```

Then each pair may be transformed.

Example:

```text
AB → BA
CD → DC
EF → FE
```

Result:

```text
BADCFE
```

Another rule:

```text
A+B
C+D
E+F
```

could produce numbers.

---

## 106. Pair Sum Coding

Example:

```text
ABCD
```

Positions:

```text
A=1
B=2
C=3
D=4
```

Pair sums:

```text
A+B = 3
C+D = 7
```

Code:

```text
3,7
```

---

## 107. Pair Difference Coding

```text
ABCD
```

Absolute differences:

```text
|1-2| = 1
|3-4| = 1
```

Code:

```text
1,1
```

---
